{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1102368-premade-adventures","id":1102368,"title":"Premade adventures","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-10T15:01:42-07:00","id":1102368,"title":"Premade adventures","content":"I'm currently running a group of friends through the Requiem demo (Danse de la Mort). We were interested in trying it out to see if we wanted to do a full chronicle with custom characters and story arcs. I'm the only one who has past experience with Vampire (although I haven't played since Masquerade), but everyone else are brand new to the setting. We've had a couple sessions and it turns out that everyone loves the game, so we are definitely going to continue. I have some ideas for story arcs, but due to a busy schedule it'll take me a while to develop them and make them playable. So, I'm interested in finding some good premade adventures I can run when I need to buy some time to finish up my own adventures. In particular a good adventure or two I can use to start the chronicle with would be really helpful. I don't mind converting from other editions of Vampire. Any suggestions would be most appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T15:37:18-07:00","id":1102386,"title":"","content":"There's a few. I think the only one available in second edition is <a href=\"http://drivethrurpg.com/product/201127/Reap-the-Whirlwind-Revised-VtR-2e\" target=\"_blank\">Reap the Whirlwind</a>. Which is a cool if chaotic introduction to vampire, specifically the political part of it. The Prince is dead! Find all his blackmail material before everyone else does!<br /> <br /> First edition had the SAS, the Storytelling Adventure System, which had a lot of premade adventures for various gamelines. You can see them <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Storytelling_Adventure_System\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> The Chicago book has one too, but that's going back to like the first books of first edition. And Requiem for Rome has the Fall of the Camarilla, though that takes place over a thousand years ago and may not be good for introducing people to Vampire unless you plan on focusing on historical periods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T17:44:46-07:00","id":1102400,"title":"","content":"<b>The Resurrectionists </b>is a good one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-10T19:57:46-07:00","id":1102417,"title":"","content":"You could also adapt WoD SASnot specifically Vampire's stories: it gives the story another twist. Even if I never tried, it might be possible to use Hunters SAS too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1851-jps","name":"JPS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}